IMPORT prelude

-- Christian Brothers' Schools Visitor Ordinance 1915 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Visitor in the Straits Settlements of the
-- Christian Brothers' Schools" is and when a successor Visitor is "duly qualified" (s 2(1), (4)), what the Gazette notification proves
-- (s 2(5)), what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do (s 2(2), (3)), how its instruments are duly sealed (s 3), which property of
-- St Joseph's and St Xavier's Institutions it took over (s 4), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CBSVO1915.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The amendment
-- annotations in the body are "[72/59]" under s 2(4) and "[7/97]" under s 5. The Ordinance is dated 17 December 1915.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0230 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Ordinance is five sections long, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside
-- the Society it matters in two places: dealing with the Corporation over property (s 2(3), s 3), and title to property that was held
-- before 1915 by the Directors of St Joseph's Institution (Singapore) or St Xavier's Institution (Penang) (s 4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the preamble (recited for context only); the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property
-- Act 1886, to which ss 2(4) and 3(1) refer (whether an instrument was filed or a power of attorney deposited under it is taken as a
-- stated fact); what "the Colony" covered and what "the respective estates and interests" in s 4 are; the Society's internal rules for
-- appointing a Visitor, about which the Ordinance says nothing beyond the preamble.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Christian Brothers' Schools Visitor Ordinance 1915 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1), 2(4) and 2(5) -- who is the Corporation, when a successor is duly qualified, and what the Gazette proves`

-- s 2(1): "The said James Joseph Byrne and his successors for the time being in the office of Visitor in the Straits Settlements of the
-- Christian Brothers' Schools duly qualified as hereinafter provided shall be a body corporate, hereinafter called the Corporation".
-- s 2(4): "No person shall be deemed to be duly qualified as aforesaid unless and until he has first, with the approval of the Minister
-- signified under his hand and seal, caused the power of attorney or other instrument constituting him such Visitor to be duly filed in
-- the Registry of the Supreme Court at Singapore, pursuant to section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, and unless and
-- until a notification of such filing has appeared in the Gazette."
-- s 2(5): "Such notification shall be sufficient evidence of the appointment and that the person therein named is duly qualified".
--
-- Three things must all be true for a successor: the Minister's approval under hand and seal, filing in the Supreme Court Registry, and a
-- Gazette notification of the filing. Brother James (James Joseph Byrne) is named in s 2(1) itself; reading the qualification in s 2(4)
-- as applying to his successors only is an inference from the grammar of s 2(1), not a statement of the text. The Gazette notification
-- is "sufficient" evidence, not "conclusive" (contrast s 5 of the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911, which says "conclusive"); the
-- encoding records only that it is evidence, and not whether it can be rebutted.
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is James Joseph Byrne` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds the office of Visitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the Minister's approval under hand and seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has filed the constituting instrument in the Supreme Court Registry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `filing is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a duly qualified successor` IF
        `the claimant`'s `holds the office of Visitor`
    AND `the claimant`'s `has the Minister's approval under hand and seal`
    AND `the claimant`'s `has filed the constituting instrument in the Supreme Court Registry`
    AND `the claimant`'s `filing is notified in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Corporation` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is James Joseph Byrne`
    OR  `is a duly qualified successor` `the claimant`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Gazette is sufficient evidence of qualification` IF
    `the claimant`'s `filing is notified in the Gazette`

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): the seal "may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as to the Corporation seems fit".
-- s 2(3): the Corporation "may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description and may sell,
-- convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable or immovable property
-- vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". Unlike the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911, s 2(3) here
-- grants no power to sue or be sued, and the Ordinance does not mention perpetual succession; whether the general law supplies either is
-- outside the text and not encoded.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `use and change its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue or be sued`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `use and change its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- when an instrument is duly sealed`

-- s 3(1): "No deed, document or other instrument sealed with the seal of the Corporation shall be deemed to be duly sealed unless such
-- seal has been affixed in the presence of the said James Joseph Byrne or his attorney duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited
-- under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, or in the presence of his successor for the time being in his said
-- office of Visitor and duly qualified as aforesaid, and unless such deed, document or other instrument is signed by the said James
-- Joseph Byrne or his attorney or by his successor or his said attorney."
-- s 3(2): "Such signing shall be taken as sufficient evidence of the due sealing of such deed, document or other instrument."
--
-- The presence limb names Byrne, Byrne's deposited attorney, and a duly qualified successor. It does not name a successor's attorney.
-- The signing limb adds "his successor or his said attorney"; reading "his said attorney" as the successor's attorney holding a
-- deposited power is an inference. So on the literal words a successor's attorney may sign but may not be the person in whose presence
-- the seal is affixed. The successor in the signing limb is read as the duly qualified successor of the presence limb (inference).
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `James Joseph Byrne`
    `Byrne's attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `a duly qualified successor Visitor`
    `a successor's attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a successor Visitor not yet gazetted`
    `a school Director with no power of attorney`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may witness the sealing` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `James Joseph Byrne` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Byrne's attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duly qualified successor Visitor` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sign` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `James Joseph Byrne` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Byrne's attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duly qualified successor Visitor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a successor's attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly sealed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness the sealing` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `may sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `4 -- property of the two Institutions vested in the Corporation`

-- s 4: "All movable and immovable property situated in the Colony heretofore held, conveyed or assigned to or vested in either the
-- Director in Singapore of St. Joseph's Institution or the Director in Penang of St. Xavier's Institution whether with or without the
-- name of the Director for the time being holding the office is hereby vested in the Corporation for the respective estates and
-- interests for which the same is held."
--
-- Movable property is swept in as well as immovable. "Heretofore" is read as before the Ordinance (17 December 1915): an inference from
-- the word, not a date the section states. Whether the property is "situated in the Colony" is taken as a stated fact. Only the two
-- named Directors count: the Director of St Joseph's in Singapore and the Director of St Xavier's in Penang.
DECLARE Holder IS ONE OF
    `the Director in Singapore of St Joseph's Institution`
    `the Director in Penang of St Xavier's Institution`
    `the Visitor personally`
    `an individual Brother`
    `a lay trustee for a school`

DECLARE Holding HAS
    `is situated in the Colony` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was held by` IS A Holder
    `was held before the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deed names the individual Director` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is one of the two named Directors` IF
    CONSIDER `the holder`
    WHEN `the Director in Singapore of St Joseph's Institution` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Director in Penang of St Xavier's Institution` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 vests it in the Corporation` IF
        `the holding`'s `is situated in the Colony`
    AND `is one of the two named Directors` (`the holding`'s `was held by`)
    AND `the holding`'s `was held before the Ordinance`

§§ `5 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 5: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government or of any body politic or corporate or of any other persons
-- except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
